Cody,

the mcp function from the multcomp package expects a named argument list,
not an array of strings: 

 iv        <- c('a','b','c')
 linfcts   <- eval(parse(text=paste("mcp(",paste(iv,'= "Tukey"
',collapse=','),')')));
 pairwise2 <- summary(glht(owobanova , linfct = linfcts));
 
