  I would actually say that this unbelievable uncertainty is more
widespread than that.  Should one do stepwise regression (or the
milder form under the rubric of "find the minimal adequate model"?
Pick a full model and stick to it?  Use model averaging?

> As far as estimating the population intercept and slope, 
> you mentioned that
> this can be difficult, but said 'You could check out the
>  'lsmeans' package.
>  Alternatively, if you set sum-to-zero contrasts for everything
> (options(contrasts=contr.sum)) the intercept should represent the
